WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.180
- Welcome back, everybody.
(audience applauding)

00:00:01.180 --> 00:00:03.739
I'm here with Dwayne Johnson.

00:00:03.739 --> 00:00:05.318
(audience cheers)

00:00:05.318 --> 00:00:06.230
All right, before the break

00:00:06.230 --> 00:00:08.660
we talked about Dwayne's
father being a wrestler.

00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:11.240
But actually his grandmother
was a groundbreaker

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:12.530
in the field as well.

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:14.560
So Dwayne, in your new show, "Young Rock"

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:16.210
you were actually able to have a hand

00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:19.610
in casting her as well
as your mother, right?

00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:21.000
- Yes, absolutely.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:25.030
And we have Ana and
Stacey who are here now.

00:00:25.030 --> 00:00:26.360
- What's up, ladies?

00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:27.193
How are you doing?

00:00:27.193 --> 00:00:29.741
Thank you so much for joining us.

00:00:29.741 --> 00:00:30.574
(audience claps)

00:00:30.574 --> 00:00:32.480
So everybody right now

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:33.820
from halfway around the world

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:35.933
here are Stacey Leilua, and Ana Tuisila.

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:37.981
Give it up!

00:00:37.981 --> 00:00:39.480
(audience applauds)

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:41.490
So where are you calling from?

00:00:41.490 --> 00:00:43.630
- So I'm calling from
Auckland, New Zealand

00:00:43.630 --> 00:00:46.130
at the moment in a quarantine facility.

00:00:46.130 --> 00:00:47.740
Just got back last week.

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:49.420
So yeah here I am.

00:00:49.420 --> 00:00:53.690
- Oh wow, what was it like
being like picked by him?

00:00:53.690 --> 00:00:54.940
Was that like,

00:00:54.940 --> 00:00:56.700
I mean it's got to be such an honor

00:00:56.700 --> 00:00:59.130
that somebody's that into what you do

00:00:59.130 --> 00:01:00.430
and then to be picked for this show

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:02.210
that represents his life.

00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:03.043
- For sure.

00:01:03.890 --> 00:01:05.630
You know, auditioning for the role

00:01:05.630 --> 00:01:07.790
and I guess you go

00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:09.210
through the normal audition process

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:13.067
and it didn't actually dawn
on me until someone said,

00:01:13.067 --> 00:01:14.197
"Hey, do you think,

00:01:14.197 --> 00:01:17.100
Dwayne's surely like casting you guys

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:18.540
because you're his family.

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:19.630
Of course he would do that."

00:01:19.630 --> 00:01:21.890
And that's when it kind of
dawned on me and I thought,

00:01:21.890 --> 00:01:24.670
oh okay, yeah, that's probably
exactly what had happened.

00:01:24.670 --> 00:01:26.950
And then that was confirmed

00:01:26.950 --> 00:01:28.380
when we chatted on our Zoom.

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:31.170
And you said you'd shown
your mom and stuff.

00:01:31.170 --> 00:01:34.250
And yeah it's just an incredible,

00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:36.260
amazing opportunity that I'm grateful

00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:37.950
for every day (chuckles).

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:39.990
- Well, Ana you want to tell us a little

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:42.310
about your character?

00:01:42.310 --> 00:01:45.653
- Yes, well, thanks for the opportunity.

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:47.753
Lia, I play Lia,

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:52.130
Dwayne Johnson's grandmother.

00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:53.570
Very little is known about her

00:01:53.570 --> 00:01:54.830
because she was very much

00:01:54.830 --> 00:01:57.010
a woman behind the scenes.

00:01:57.010 --> 00:01:59.370
But she was a very strong woman.

00:01:59.370 --> 00:02:02.510
A very strong woman with no holds barred.

00:02:02.510 --> 00:02:06.900
She was feared but she was well-respected

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:09.720
and loved by all.

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:12.770
She worked very hard to ensure

00:02:12.770 --> 00:02:16.150
that she lived on her husband's dream.

00:02:16.150 --> 00:02:19.908
And that was very hard in terms of working

00:02:19.908 --> 00:02:23.013
in a male-dominated sport,

00:02:24.350 --> 00:02:25.710
particularly doing wrestling.

00:02:25.710 --> 00:02:28.960
So she was tough and she had to be

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:33.960
in order to succeed where
wrestling field is now.

00:02:34.942 --> 00:02:39.520
- Kelly, if I could jump in and say that

00:02:40.740 --> 00:02:43.120
when we talked about
how it's just so surreal

00:02:43.120 --> 00:02:44.850
this entire process has been for me.

00:02:44.850 --> 00:02:46.370
I've never experienced anything like this

00:02:46.370 --> 00:02:47.890
in my entire career.

00:02:47.890 --> 00:02:50.420
And I probably won't experience

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:51.600
anything like this ever again,

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:53.890
just in terms of taking a look back

00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:57.390
at my life and all these
defining moments and times

00:02:57.390 --> 00:02:59.640
and struggling times and the
intersections that I've had

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:04.640
in my wild life growing up
and now to be able to cast

00:03:07.830 --> 00:03:09.450
Ana and Stacey.

00:03:09.450 --> 00:03:10.283
As you know,

00:03:10.283 --> 00:03:13.470
my grandmother and my mom
were the pillars of my life.

00:03:13.470 --> 00:03:17.450
And I was raised by strong
women, by both of them.

00:03:17.450 --> 00:03:21.430
And this incredible job that
Stacey has done playing my mom

00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:23.830
but also that Ana has done
playing my grandmother.

00:03:23.830 --> 00:03:26.510
Just so you know, Kelly and your audience,

00:03:26.510 --> 00:03:29.370
my grandmother was the first
female wrestling promoter.

00:03:29.370 --> 00:03:33.290
And if you think about
it, in the '70s and '80s,

00:03:33.290 --> 00:03:36.250
how wrestling was as a culture

00:03:36.250 --> 00:03:39.720
and then on top of that, you
throw a woman into the mix.

00:03:39.720 --> 00:03:40.860
Then on top of that, you throw a woman

00:03:40.860 --> 00:03:42.450
into the mix who is
going to be a promoter.

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:45.320
Who's telling these wrestlers
what they're going to do

00:03:45.320 --> 00:03:47.490
and who's going to win
and who's going to lose.

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:50.630
And how incredibly difficult that was.

00:03:50.630 --> 00:03:55.010
So she promoted with an iron fist

00:03:55.010 --> 00:03:58.960
and she was not taking any
you know what off of anybody

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:02.620
she was incredibly tough
and she had to be tough.

00:04:02.620 --> 00:04:04.500
And then, eventually

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:07.370
and this is documented, we
documented this in the show,

00:04:07.370 --> 00:04:08.750
she was so tough

00:04:08.750 --> 00:04:11.030
that the feds actually bought her up

00:04:11.030 --> 00:04:12.740
on extortion charges (laughs).

00:04:12.740 --> 00:04:14.770
Now that's a whole other story,

00:04:14.770 --> 00:04:19.580
but what they were able
to do, Stacey and Ana

00:04:19.580 --> 00:04:22.160
and really ground and bring my mom

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:25.600
and my grandmother to life
was just really extraordinary.

00:04:25.600 --> 00:04:27.800
So I really, I just want to take a moment

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:30.700
to give it up to these incredible women.

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:31.813
I'm just so grateful.

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:34.620
And when you see them in our show

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:37.685
and the performances they
give are just phenomenal.

00:04:37.685 --> 00:04:38.518
(audience applauds)

00:04:38.518 --> 00:04:39.351
- I can't, oh my gosh.

00:04:39.351 --> 00:04:41.070
Like, I mean, as an actor,

00:04:41.070 --> 00:04:43.410
like I can't imagine Ana getting to play.

00:04:43.410 --> 00:04:46.090
I say character, obviously
it's a real person,

00:04:46.090 --> 00:04:47.739
but to play a character like that,

00:04:47.739 --> 00:04:49.650
such a bold woman.

00:04:49.650 --> 00:04:54.170
I can imagine it's
probably still to this day,

00:04:54.170 --> 00:04:57.380
male dominated when it comes
to promoting wrestling.

00:04:57.380 --> 00:04:58.680
I mean, it's probably still there.

00:04:58.680 --> 00:04:59.513
That's what I'm saying.

00:04:59.513 --> 00:05:01.810
So it's still a pioneer
kind of thing to do.

00:05:01.810 --> 00:05:05.140
So to play that kind of
role has to be incredible.

00:05:05.140 --> 00:05:06.570
What an opportunity to just get

00:05:06.570 --> 00:05:09.953
to play someone so bold and strong.

